# Secrets
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# The agent's filesystem root. Everything in it is ignored except what is
# tracked on purpose: the skills, and the .gitkeep that holds workspace/ open.
#
# This is an allowlist because the libraries decide where they write, and a
# folder nobody listed must be ignored by default, never committed by default.
# What lands here today, all of it household data:
#   workspace/            the user's uploaded statements
#   AGENTS.md             the household profile the agent maintains (income,
#                         balances, goals, account details); recreated from a
#                         template on first run
#   conversation_history/ turns the Deep Agents summarizer removed from context
#   large_tool_results/   tool results over the token limit, which
#                         FilesystemMiddleware evicts instead of returning
# The last two are written by different middleware for different reasons, and
# both go through the on-disk backend, whose "/" virtual_mode re-roots here.
#
# Paths must be spelled in full: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to
# the directory holding this .gitignore, so a bare "workspace/*" would only
# match a top-level workspace/ and would silently fail to cover this one.
#
# Order matters: git cannot re-include a path whose parent is excluded, so the
# first line excludes agent_home's contents (not agent_home/ itself), and
# workspace/ is re-included before its own contents are excluded again.
agent_home/*
!agent_home/skills/
!agent_home/workspace/
agent_home/workspace/*
!agent_home/workspace/.gitkeep

# Persisted cross-session memory (SQLite store/checkpointer)
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

.DS_Store
